        "## Handle class imbalance\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Addressing the class imbalance in the training set using appropriate techniques (e.g., oversampling or undersampling).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "44b26c75"
      },
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "Applying SMOTE to the training data to address class imbalance and print the value counts before and after applying SMOTE to show the effect.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ed2cac0d",
        "outputId": "80c7001f-8d98-4b29-9c0c-ce48322e5c8b"
      },
      "source": [
        "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print the value counts of the original y_train\n",
        "print(\"Original y_train value counts:\")\n",
        "print(y_train.value_counts())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Instantiate SMOTE\n",
        "smote = SMOTE(random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply SMOTE to the training data\n",
        "X_train_resampled, y_train_resampled = smote.fit_resample(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print the value counts of the resampled y_train\n",
        "print(\"\\nResampled y_train value counts:\")\n",
        "print(y_train_resampled.value_counts())"
