        "## Insight into Feature Extraction and Model Combination Performance\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on the feature selection performed using `SelectKBest` and the subsequent training and evaluation of multiple traditional machine learning models on the dataset with the selected features, we can draw the following conclusions:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Feature Extraction Method:**\n",
        "\n",
        "*   We applied **feature selection** using `SelectKBest` with the `f_classif` score function to reduce the dimensionality of the numerical features. The top 5 features selected were 'Protein', 'Sugar', 'Sodium', 'Cholesterol', and 'Serving\\_Size'.\n",
        "*   The feature importance scores indicated that 'Sodium', 'Serving\\_Size', and 'Cholesterol' were the most influential features among the numerical ones for classifying food types.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Model Performance:**\n",
        "\n",
        "*   We trained and evaluated seven different traditional machine learning classifiers: Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, K-Nearest Neighbors, Support Vector Machine, XGBoost, and Gradient Boosting Classifier.\n",
        "*   The models were trained on the resampled training data (to address class imbalance) and evaluated on the original testing set.\n",
        "*   Based on the performance metrics (Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score), the **XGBoost classifier** consistently showed the highest performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Best Performing Combination:**\n",
        "\n",
        "*   The combination that performed best in this analysis is using **feature selection (SelectKBest with the top 5 features)** followed by training an **XGBoost classifier** on the data with these selected features (along with the one-hot encoded categorical features) and using **SMOTE for handling class imbalance**.\n",
        "\n",
        "This combination yielded the highest F1-score, which is a good indicator of a model's performance on imbalanced datasets as it considers both precision and recall. The high accuracy, precision, and recall values for XGBoost further support its effectiveness for this classification task with the chosen features.\n",
        "\n",
        "While this analysis provides valuable insight, further exploration could involve:\n",
        "\n",
        "*   Experimenting with a different number of selected features.\n",
        "*   Trying other feature selection methods.\n",
        "*   Performing hyperparameter tuning on the best-performing XGBoost model to potentially improve its performance further."
